# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# `go mod vendor` output must be committed in full. The binary and coverage
# patterns above (*.exe, *.dll, coverage.*) otherwise silently drop vendored
# third-party files, such as x/text/.../coverage.go and the Windows WebView2
# loaders. A clean checkout then fails the production build. This negation
# keeps every vendored file tracked.
!vendor/**

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Deferred worktree-teardown trash dirs (§7.2). The cleanup script removes
# them. Ignored here in case a run or test stops mid-teardown.
.perch_trash_*/

# Build output
/bin/
# Root binary from an ad-hoc `go build ./cmd/perch` (canonical build goes to /bin via `make build`)
/perch
# Stray fake-agent binary (test builds it to a temp dir; ignore any accidental root-level copy)
/fake-agent

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Playwright e2e artifacts (specs are tracked; run output and screenshots are not)
frontend/test-results/
frontend/e2e/__screenshots__/
frontend/playwright-report/

frontend/node_modules/
# frontend/dist/ is ignored as a whole. Vite build output is not committed.
# Exception: frontend/dist/index.html is intentionally tracked as the go:embed
# stub that Wails embeds into the production binary. To commit the stub, use
# `git add -f frontend/dist/index.html` (or it stays tracked once committed).
frontend/dist/
frontend/wailsjs/
build/bin/
frontend/package.json.md5

# brainstorm visual companion
.superpowers/
